// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_SECRET_EXFILTRATION
// CONFIDENTIALITY missed-leak (place-assignment laundering, the dual of the taint case): a secret value
// stored into a container element via a non-`Var` target (`a[0] = k`) must label the whole container
// secret, so egressing `a` over the network is exfiltration. Before the fix the confidentiality update
// was gated on `Expr::Var` targets, so `a` stayed clean and `send(host, port, a)` transmitted the secret
// while the check passed green. The fix MAY-labels the assignment root secret (set-only) for a non-`Var`
// place.
fn main() uses(net.send) {
    let k: secret<u64> = 42424242;
    let a = [0, 0];
    a[0] = k;
    send("127.0.0.1", 9931, a);
}
